The thing is you need to get the same random number to seed the level
generator; for this purpose you could, at the beginning of the game,
generate 60 random numbers and use those for generating the level
layout -- however, that means using one stream of random numbers
for gameplay, and another (from each of those 60-odd seeds) for
level generation. This presumes, though, that the interesting
bit of each level is the layout of the dungeon and the items
that it is pre-stocked with, and not the beasts that inhabit
the level.

Perhaps we need to go back and wonder what the OP actually wanted:

1. The layout of the dungeon levels 1..Sanctum to be the same for
   each player?
2. The items on the floor on those levels to be the same for each player?
3. The monsters generated on those levels ... ?

ad 3 there is the obvious problem of players entering the level
at different XLs, which would cause different monster generation
under the current code, and cause undue hardship if the "presumed"
XL is included -- makes the protection racket much harder if
DL n gets DIF n monsters instead of DIF n/2, that kind of thing.

In any case you quickly get the fact that the games get out of
sync because player KPD camps on level one for 30000 turns,
while player M ascends twice in that number :)



